Date: 2025-08-31

Understanding:
- Implement an AI controller for the Need4Stek simulator: parse LIDAR frames and output driving commands (speed, steering) according to obstacles.

Strategy:
- Read lines on stdin; when a line starts with "LIDAR:", parse numerical values, compute a simple rule-based control (speed depends on forward clearance; steer towards the widest side), and print commands.

What I did:
- Wrote a small C AI loop with helpers `parse_lidar` and `compute_controls`, plus a CLI `./ai`. Added Criterion tests for parsing and control logic and a standard Makefile with tests/coverage.

